---
import ComparisonTable from "@components/article/ComparisonTable.astro";
import FAQSection from "@components/article/FAQSection.astro";
import RelatedArticles from "@components/article/RelatedArticles.astro";
import ArticleLayout from "../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro";

// Article metadata
const title = "Crypto-Friendly Banks for Remote Workers (2025)";
const description =
  "Some banks will freeze your account the moment they see Coinbase or Binance transactions. It happened to me twice. Here's which banks work with crypto.";
const authorSlug = "daniel-brooks";
const pubDate = new Date("2025-11-23");
const readingTime = 3;
const image = "/images/unsplash/photo-1518546305927-5a555bb7020d-1200w.webp";
const imageAlt = "Bitcoin and cryptocurrency concept with digital technology";

// Table of contents
const headings = [
  { text: "The Problem", slug: "introduction", depth: 2 },
  { text: "Quick Comparison", slug: "quick-comparison", depth: 2 },
  { text: "Why Banks Hate Crypto", slug: "why-banks-block", depth: 2 },
  { text: "The Good Options", slug: "best-options", depth: 2 },
  { text: "How to Not Get Banned", slug: "best-practices", depth: 2 },
  { text: "FAQ", slug: "faq", depth: 2 },
  { text: "Bottom Line", slug: "conclusion", depth: 2 },
];

// Comparison table
const comparisonColumns = [
  { key: "bank", label: "Bank", width: "110px" },
  { key: "type", label: "Type" },
  { key: "crypto", label: "Crypto Friendly" },
  { key: "transfers", label: "Exchange Transfers" },
  { key: "notes", label: "Notes" },
];

const comparisonRows = [
  {
    bank: "<strong>Revolut</strong>",
    type: "Digital",
    crypto: "Built-in",
    transfers: "Yes",
    notes: "Buy/sell crypto in-app",
  },
  {
    bank: "<strong>Ally Bank</strong>",
    type: "Traditional",
    crypto: "Tolerant",
    transfers: "Yes",
    notes: "US only, no issues reported",
  },
  {
    bank: "<strong>Fidelity</strong>",
    type: "Brokerage",
    crypto: "Supports",
    transfers: "Yes",
    notes: "Bitcoin in retirement accounts",
  },
  {
    bank: "<strong>Mercury</strong>",
    type: "Business",
    crypto: "Business OK",
    transfers: "Yes",
    notes: "Crypto business friendly",
  },
  {
    bank: "<strong>Juno</strong>",
    type: "Digital",
    crypto: "Built-in",
    transfers: "Yes",
    notes: "Crypto checking account",
  },
];

// FAQ data
const faqs = [
  {
    question: "Can they close my account for buying crypto?",
    answer:
      "<p>Yes. Happens more with large or frequent transfers. Using the right banks and not being sketchy minimizes risk.</p>",
  },
  {
    question: "Should I tell my bank?",
    answer: "<p>No need to volunteer. If they ask, be honest. Crypto investing is legal.</p>",
  },
  {
    question: "Best way to cash out?",
    answer:
      "<p>Sell on Coinbase/Kraken/Gemini, withdraw to bank. Smaller regular withdrawals beat one huge transfer. Or use a crypto debit card.</p>",
  },
  {
    question: "Are crypto banks safe?",
    answer:
      "<p>Be careful with newer ones. Check FDIC insurance. Several have failed. Only keep what you're using.</p>",
  },
  {
    question: "Do I pay taxes on crypto?",
    answer:
      "<p>Yes. Treated as property in the US. Capital gains when you sell. Keep records. Use Koinly or CoinTracker.</p>",
  },
];

// Related articles
const relatedArticles = [
  {
    title: "Best Banking for Digital Nomads",
    excerpt: "Multi-currency accounts and low-fee banking for international living.",
    href: "/blog/best-banking-digital-nomads",
    image: "/images/unsplash/photo-1563986768494-4dee2763ff3f-800w.webp",
    imageAlt: "Mobile banking app",
  },
  {
    title: "Tax Tips for Remote Workers",
    excerpt: "Navigate taxes including crypto reporting as a digital nomad.",
    href: "/blog/tax-tips-remote-workers",
    image: "/images/unsplash/photo-1554224155-6726b3ff858f-800w.webp",
    imageAlt: "Tax documents",
  },
  {
    title: "Best VPN for Digital Nomads",
    excerpt: "Secure your crypto transactions while traveling.",
    href: "/tools/best-vpn-digital-nomads",
    image: "/images/unsplash/photo-1526374965328-7f61d4dc18c5-800w.webp",
    imageAlt: "VPN security",
  },
];
---

<ArticleLayout
    title={title}
    description={description}
    authorSlug={authorSlug}
    pubDate={pubDate}
    readingTime={readingTime}
    image={image}
    imageAlt={imageAlt}
    category="Finance"
    categorySlug="tools/finance"
    headings={headings}
>
  <!-- Introduction -->
  <h2 id="introduction">The Problem</h2>
  <p>
    Crypto is legal. Banks act like it isn't.
  </p>
  <p>
    Transfer money to Coinbase? Flagged. Cash out from an exchange? Frozen. Do it too often? Account closed. No warning.
  </p>
  <p>
    I've seen it happen to friends. One guy had his Chase account shut down after three Coinbase transfers. No
    explanation. Just gone.
  </p>
  <p>
    Not all banks are like this. Some tolerate crypto. Some embrace it. A few even have it built in. You just need to
    know which ones.
  </p>

  <!-- Quick Comparison -->
  <h2 id="quick-comparison">Quick Comparison</h2>

  <ComparisonTable columns={comparisonColumns} rows={comparisonRows}/>

  <p>
    <strong>My picks:</strong> Revolut if you want crypto built in. Ally if you want traditional banking that won't
    hassle you. Mercury if you're running a crypto business.
  </p>

  <!-- Why Banks Block Crypto -->
  <h2 id="why-banks-block">Why Banks Hate Crypto</h2>
  <p>
    Compliance teams are terrified. Money laundering regulations are strict. Crypto is pseudonymous. Easier to just ban
    everything than risk a regulatory nightmare.
  </p>
  <p>
    They also see fraud reports constantly. Doesn't matter if the exchange wasn't at fault—they get spooked.
  </p>
  <p>
    And sudden large transfers look suspicious to automated systems. $50K appearing overnight? Fraud alert.
  </p>

  <h3>Banks That Block Crypto</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Chase:</strong> Has blocked purchases</li>
    <li><strong>Bank of America:</strong> Restricts some transfers</li>
    <li><strong>Wells Fargo:</strong> History of problems</li>
    <li><strong>Citibank:</strong> Declines transactions</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Policies change. Your mileage may vary. But these have reputations.
  </p>

  <!-- Best Options -->
  <h2 id="best-options">The Good Options</h2>

  <h3>Banks With Crypto Built In</h3>

  <h4 id="revolut">Revolut</h4>
  <p>
    Buy and sell 100+ cryptos in the app. No external exchange needed. Withdraw to wallets on paid plans.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What I like:</strong> Everything in one place. No suspicious transfers because it's all internal.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What's annoying:</strong> Premium plan for external withdrawals.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/go/revolut" rel="nofollow sponsored" class="text-jet-stream hover:text-sky-light">
      Open Revolut Account &rarr;
    </a>
  </p>

  <h4 id="juno">Juno</h4>
  <p>
    Checking account for crypto people. Earn yield on stablecoins. Easy conversion to USD.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What I like:</strong> FDIC insured (the USD part). Clean bridge between crypto and fiat.
  </p>

  <h3>Traditional Banks That Don't Care</h3>

  <h4 id="ally">Ally Bank</h4>
  <p>
    Online bank. Consistently positive reports from <a href="/guides/productivity">crypto users</a>. Coinbase, Kraken
    transfers—no problems.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What I like:</strong> Traditional bank that just... lets you do crypto stuff.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What's annoying:</strong> US only.
  </p>

  <h4 id="fidelity">Fidelity</h4>
  <p>
    Big brokerage embracing crypto. Bitcoin in 401(k)s. Generally friendly.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What I like:</strong> Crypto in <a href="/blog/tax-tips-remote-workers">retirement accounts</a>. Legitimacy.
  </p>

  <h3>Business Banking</h3>

  <h4 id="mercury">Mercury</h4>
  <p>
    Modern <a href="/guides/freelancer-tax-deductions-guide">business banking</a> that actually accepts crypto
    companies. Web3 startups, exchanges—they'll work with you.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What I like:</strong> One of the few options if your business involves crypto.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/go/mercury" rel="nofollow sponsored" class="text-jet-stream hover:text-sky-light">
      Open Mercury Account &rarr;
    </a>
  </p>

  <h3>Crypto-Native Options</h3>
  <p>
    Not banks, but banking-like:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Coinbase Card:</strong> Spend crypto anywhere Visa works</li>
    <li><strong>Crypto.com:</strong> Metal cards, rewards</li>
    <li><strong>Nexo:</strong> Earn interest, borrow against holdings</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Warning:</strong> Not FDIC insured. Only keep what you're actively using.
  </p>

  <!-- Best Practices -->
  <h2 id="best-practices">How to Not Get Banned</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Use legit exchanges.</strong> Banks know Coinbase. They don't know random DEX #47.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Avoid huge sudden transfers.</strong> $50K appearing overnight looks sketchy. Spread it out.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong><a href="/blog/tax-tips-remote-workers">Keep records</a>.</strong> If they ask, you want to show legitimate
    investing, not money laundering.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Use separate accounts.</strong> Keep crypto activity in one bank. If it gets restricted, your main banking
    survives.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Don't lie.</strong> If they ask about transactions, be honest. Lying creates way bigger problems.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Have backups.</strong> Always <a href="/blog/best-banking-digital-nomads">multiple banks</a>. Never be
    stranded.
  </p>

  <!-- FAQ Section -->
  <FAQSection faqs={faqs}/>

  <!-- Conclusion -->
  <h2 id="conclusion">Bottom Line</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/go/revolut" rel="nofollow sponsored">Revolut</a> if you want crypto built into your banking.
    Ally if you want traditional banking that tolerates crypto.
    <a href="/go/mercury" rel="nofollow sponsored">Mercury</a> if you're running a crypto business.
  </p>
  <p>
    Keep a separate crypto-free account for stability. Follow the rules. Don't be sketchy.
  </p>
  <p>
    The landscape is improving. More banks are figuring this out. Pick the right ones and you'll be fine.
  </p>
  <p>
    For broader nomad banking needs, see our guide to
    <a href="/blog/best-banking-digital-nomads">banking for digital nomads</a>.
  </p>

  <!-- Related Articles -->
  <Fragment slot="full-width">
    <RelatedArticles articles={relatedArticles}/>
  </Fragment>
</ArticleLayout>
